{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435538-core-changing-favored-approach","id":1435538,"title":"[Core] Changing favored approach","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-15T04:34:28-08:00","id":1435538,"title":"[Core] Changing favored approach","content":"The XP table defines a 15xp cost for changing your favores approach.<br /> <br /> I don't understand the usefullness of this.<br /> What does it do?<br /> It changes the attribute dots assigned to your favored approach to the new one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T05:20:38-08:00","id":1435996,"title":"","content":"Ok, I get it.<br /> <br /> No one knows.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T05:48:52-08:00","id":1435998,"title":"","content":"It does what it says, moves your favored approach, which would entail moving the dots it gives to your new approach attributes. However, you can also spend 3 sessions tweaking your character to do the same thing, so no one ever does it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T08:59:31-08:00","id":1436020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vjornin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435538-core-changing-favored-approach?p=1435996#post1435996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I get it.<br /> <br /> No one knows.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Like Florin said, that is this simple and nobody uses.<br /> <br /> Basically we gave up in giving it a meaning/significance because it doesn\u2019t add to our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T10:06:40-08:00","id":1436032,"title":"","content":"I never thought of it like. Yea, it doesn't do much because you can move dots around after a session. Weird....that feels like an artifact of early drafts that just stuck around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T10:09:29-08:00","id":1436033,"title":"","content":"That or someone at OPP is like, &quot;Just wait until they figure out why we put it in there. It's going to blow their minds!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T12:51:14-08:00","id":1436065,"title":"","content":"I figure the Favored Approach must have originally given some sort of significant bonus, such as a 9-again rule, lowered difficulty on dice rolls, bonus Momentum, etcetera. Either the bonus was unbalanced, people got frustrated over consistently forgetting to apply the rule, or people were using their Favored Approach Attributes for every single dice roll possible, so the entire thing was dropped. For example, if your Favored Approach is Force and you max your Force stats, you can just bull your way through the campaign and get a free bonus to virtually everything you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T14:15:42-08:00","id":1436070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435538-core-changing-favored-approach?p=1436065#post1436065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure the Favored Approach must have originally given some sort of significant bonus, such as a 9-again rule, lowered difficulty on dice rolls, bonus Momentum, etcetera. Either the bonus was unbalanced, people got frustrated over consistently forgetting to apply the rule, or people were using their Favored Approach Attributes for every single dice roll possible, so the entire thing was dropped. For example, if your Favored Approach is Force and you max your Force stats, you can just bull your way through the campaign and get a free bonus to virtually everything you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is probably the best explanation. The first time I read it was not like this, but Storypath has a long development story, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T03:55:33-08:00","id":1436532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435538-core-changing-favored-approach?p=1436065#post1436065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure the Favored Approach must have originally given some sort of significant bonus, such as a 9-again rule, lowered difficulty on dice rolls, bonus Momentum, etcetera. Either the bonus was unbalanced, people got frustrated over consistently forgetting to apply the rule, or people were using their Favored Approach Attributes for every single dice roll possible, so the entire thing was dropped. For example, if your Favored Approach is Force and you max your Force stats, you can just bull your way through the campaign and get a free bonus to virtually everything you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also thought this, So, I asked to know if somewhere there was a rule I missed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T11:14:53-08:00","id":1436845,"title":"","content":"Here's what it does: it makes you lose 15 xp. There's nothing like it! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}